{
    "format": "lumiviz-instrument-body",
    "version": 8,
    "title": "Classical guitar",
    "description": "Measured body: modal fit to guitar g34 of the Mores archive (Manuel Contreras, Madrid 1971, cedar / Rio palisander, scale 662 mm). Six bridge points, one per open string; two listening points 10 cm above the top plate (near field); above 5 kHz a statistical part fitted to the measurement. Above 2.2 kHz modes are drawn up to the modal density after Elie 2011; the direction at the bridge and the in-plane modes follow Elie 2012. See classical_guitar.lvinstbodyfit.",
    "units": "f in Hz; eta loss factor; bridge: mode shape at the bridge point along the direction of bridgeAngle, 1/sqrt(kg) (modal mass 1/value^2); bridgeAngle: direction in which the mode moves the bridge, degrees from the normal of the top plate, across the strings (normal component bridge * cos, in-plane component bridge * sin; 90 = in-plane only); radiation: complex pressure per modal acceleration at the listening point, sqrt(kg)/m^2 (fitted to the measured pressure per force)",
